// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`trace command (ADR-477) > prints its help text 1`] = `
"Usage: kerfdesk-trace [options] [input]

Trace a raster image to vector artwork with the KerfDesk tracer, headless.
Reads PNG, JPEG, BMP, TIFF (first page) or PBM/PGM/PPM from the input file,
or from standard input when the input is "-" or omitted. Writes to the
output file, or to standard output when it is "-" or omitted.

Output matches the app's Multi-File Trace for 8-bit sRGB PNG, BMP and Netpbm
images up to 2048 px on the long edge. JPEG decodes with a different IDCT and
chroma upsampling than the browser, and colour profiles (ICC, gAMA) are not
applied, so edge pixels of such images can trace slightly differently.

Options:
  -o, --output <file>           Output file (default: standard output)
  -p, --preset <name>           Trace preset (default: Line Art)
  -f, --format <format>         Output format: svg, dxf, pdf, eps, geojson (default: svg)
  -r, --dpi <n>[x<n>]           Image density, 10 to 10000 (default: embedded, else 254)
  --precision <mm>              Coordinate grid of the file, 0.000001 to 1 (default: 0.001)
  --group-contours              Group each colour into one path
  --page <image|artwork>        Page: the whole image, or the artwork (default: image)
  --margin <mm>                 Space around the artwork page, 0 to 1000 (default: 0)
  -h, --help                    Show this help

Trace settings (the Trace dialog controls; unset ones keep the preset value).
Values outside the range are refused. Switches take --flag, --no-flag or
--flag=true|false. Pixel counts and lengths are pixels of the image, as the
dialog sees them for images up to 2048 px on the long edge; larger images
trace at full resolution with those settings scaled as the app's finer
commit grid scales them.
  --cutoff <value>              Cutoff: darkest luma counted as ink (0 to 255)
  --threshold <value>           Threshold: lightest luma counted as ink (0 to 255)
  --ignore-less-than <value>    Ignore shapes under N pixels (0 to 10000)
  --smoothness <value>          Smoothness (0 to 1.33)
  --optimize <value>            Optimize: curve fit tolerance (0 to 2)
  --diagonal-contacts <value>   Diagonal contacts (auto, connect-ink, connect-paper)
  --[no-]invert                 Trace light artwork on a dark ground
  --detection <value>           Ink detection (preset, manual, sketch, faint-lines)
  --despeckle <value>           Remove specks under N pixels (0 to 10000)
  --[no-]fill-pinholes          Close pinholes and hairline cracks
  --[no-]trace-transparency     Trace the alpha mask
  --[no-]sketch                 Sketch (pencil) detection
  --edge-sensitivity <value>    Edge Detection sensitivity (0 to 100)
  --edge-detail <value>         Edge Detection detail (0 to 100)
  --edge-min-line <value>       Edge Detection shortest line in px (0 to 1000)
  --max-stroke-width <value>    Line + fill max stroke in mm (0.05 to 3)
  --photo-detail <value>        Photo shading detail (0 to 100)
  --photo-brightness <value>    Photo shading brightness (-100 to 100)
  --photo-contrast <value>      Photo shading contrast (-100 to 100)
  --photo-gamma <value>         Photo shading gamma (0.1 to 5)
  --[no-]photo-invert           Photo shading invert
  --colours <value>             Colour layers count (2 to 8, or auto)
  --colour-output <value>       Colour layers output style (cut-out, stacked)
  --[no-]keep-background        Colour layers: keep the background

Presets: Line Art, Photo shading, Smooth, Sharp, Centerline, Line + fill, Edge Detection, Colour layers.
Preset names ignore case; dashes or underscores may stand for spaces.

Exit status: 0 traced, 1 the image could not be read or traced,
2 invalid options, 3 the trace found nothing to draw.
"
`;
